## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic **`MiniGridPreview`** feature view at parity with the web source `features/dashboard/components/MiniGridPreview.tsx`.

**What it is:** a presentational dashboard-layout thumbnail. The web source is pure-presentational (no hooks/charts/maps), so — following the established `HighlightCard`(0076)/`ToolCard`(0010) precedent — the remote loading/error/stale/offline phases belong to the data-bound caller; the surface reproduces exactly the branches the source owns.

**7 files (1079 Swift + 27 strings), allowed scope only:**
- `MiniGridPreview.Model.swift` — pure projection: `GRID_COLS.lg=4`, the `maxY⇒safeMaxY` guard, per-item `x/cols`·`y/safeMaxY` fractional rects, the `widget.id↔item.i` join, aspect ratio, empty/count + P1/S10 strings facade + a11y seam
- `MiniGridPreview.Catalog.swift` — `MiniGridIconResolving` seam (native analogue of the shared `getWidgetDef`) + the **full 118-id** widget→SF-Symbol catalog (lucide-faithful); unknown id ⇒ nil
- `MiniGridPreview.swift` — GeometryReader absolute layout mapping the web percentage rects onto an aspect-fitted frame, friendly empty state, `view.opened` telemetry, a11y container
- `.Telemetry.swift`, `.Previews.swift`, `.Tests.swift`, `.strings`

